<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><i>Earnout
Liability</i></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company estimates the fair value of the earnout liability using a Monte Carlo simulation model that utilizes significant assumptions,
including volatility, expected term and risk-free rate that determine the probability of achieving the earnout conditions. The following
table summarizes the assumptions used in estimating the fair value of the earnout liability at the respective dates:</span></p>

